# --ion-model analytic vs measured A/B on the W2 rho2M vertical point.
# Work-list item 1 of HANDOFF_S3_ION_2026-08-09.md: does the FINE SHAPE of the
# S3 v2 measured i_ion template carry the rise-time floor, or is the floor set
# by f_ion (~0.9) alone?
#
# ONE new point. The `measured` arm already exists as DIAGNOSIS_noisefix
# (verified 2026-08-09: ion_model = measured, pzc_residual_beta = 0.75,
# noise_det3_satscan_feu07.json, greens_comb_w2_rho2M_dk50um_g19um.npz), so
# this is a single-variable swap against it — same kernel, same calib, same
# noise, same beta, same clusters.
#
# WHAT THE TWO ARMS ACTUALLY ARE (read off the inputs, not assumed):
#   measured  f_ion 0.9006, ion charge 50/90/99 % by 171.5 / 309.9 / 357.2 ns,
#             electron current spread over ~6-9 ns (drift to the ESL).
#   analytic  f_ion 0.9077 (= 1 - 13.84/150), ion current a 306.1 ns RECTANGLE
#             from t = 0, electron a prompt delta.
# A rectangle of length T puts 50/90/99 % of its charge at 0.50/0.90/0.99 T =
# 153.1 / 275.5 / 303.1 ns, so ANALYTIC IS THE FASTER OF THE TWO by 11 % at the
# ion median and 18 % at the 99 % point, on an almost identical f_ion.
#
# PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION (written before the job ran, 2026-08-09):
#   The X-view 10-90 % rise p5 moves from 254 ns (measured arm) to 230-248 ns.
#   That is a 2-10 % shift -- nowhere near the data's 150 ns -- so the template's
#   fine shape is NOT load-bearing and f_ion is what has to be wrong.
# FALSIFIER: if analytic p5 lands below ~200 ns, the ~12 % template speed
#   difference is producing a ~20 % rise change, the rise is hypersensitive to
#   the template's time profile, and item 2 of the work list (re-deriving the
#   template's species/mobility) becomes the priority over f_ion.
# NULL RESULT IS ALSO INFORMATIVE: |dp5| < 5 ns means neither the 0.7 % f_ion
#   difference nor the 11 % speed difference registers, and the rise floor is
#   insensitive to everything except the PRESENCE of the ion term -- which
#   points at f_ion needing to be wrong by a LOT, not by a little.
universe                = vanilla
executable              = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/run_stageBC_w2.sh
MY.SendCredential       = true
request_cpus            = 4
request_memory          = 16000
+MaxRuntime             = 7200
log                     = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/w2.log

NOISE = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/calib/noise_det3_satscan_feu07.json

arguments               = "rho2M DIAGNOSIS_ionanalytic $(NOISE) '' '--ion-model analytic'"
output                  = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_ionanalytic.out
error                   = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_ionanalytic.err
queue
